GGML packing layouts and scalar decoding equations were checked against ggml
revision 4bf5f6000653b7881d00963cd6ddb665ccd62a8d. Kuno's reader and decoding
implementation are safe Rust; no ggml library or C/C++ engine is linked.

IQ3_XXS, IQ4_NL and IQ4_XS scalar packing/decoding and nonlinear codebooks were
checked against llama.cpp tag b11232, ggml/src/ggml-common.h and
ggml/src/ggml-quants.c. IQ3's 256-entry grid and IQ4's nonlinear values are
derived from those MIT-licensed GGML tables. The public synthetic fixture
generator compiles extracted upstream dequantizers for development validation;
Kuno runtime and Rust tests do not link or invoke that C reference. Pinned
source SHA256 values and fixture hashes are recorded in
tests/fixtures/iq-b11232/receipt.json.

IQ2_S, IQ3_S, Q5_K and ID42 Q2_0 layouts/scalar equations and the IQ2_S
1024-entry/IQ3_S 512-entry public grids are derived from the same MIT-licensed
llama.cpp b11232 GGML sources. Native packed AVX2 execution preserves these
original scalar scale round points, F32 activations and the original 64-lane
separate multiply/add reduction. No upstream inference engine is linked.
The independent synthetic C reference's exact source/fixture hashes and geometry
are recorded in tests/fixtures/daslab-b11232/receipt.json. C and Python are
used only to regenerate committed development fixtures, not by Kuno runtime.

MTP's KV-only teacher-forced cache preparation is an independent split of the
existing Rust reference graph. The front-only/catch-up mechanism was inspected
in MIT-licensed Strata revision fb58e0dbc8399662c0e47c76578c6e878b14f6cf,
src/core/mtp.cpp. Strata's accepted-prefix recurrence replay is documented as a
future native implementation reference; its code is not linked or copied into
Kuno's execution path. Exact source locations and outstanding owner gates are
recorded in docs/kuno-native-mtp-prefix-notes.md at the repository root.

The explicit Strata Q2 MTP GGUF profile's tensor inventory, fused gate/up row
order, Gemma norm convention and split input projections were checked against
the same MIT Strata v0.1.41 revision, tools/mtp_pack.py, tools/mtp_rt.py and
sycl/src/core/mtp.cpp. Kuno's original-packed reader, equations and tests are
Rust; neither Strata's runtime engine nor its Python tools execute here. The
GGUF source manifest field is provenance, not a whole-artifact integrity hash.

Qwen35 pretokenizer/special-token semantics were checked against llama.cpp
revision 806eee9841de5f2c20f9d43914117f157d2baacc, src/llama-vocab.cpp, and
Strata revision 6f32ec070f23ced9f50e704d854d775da52591ab,
tools/strata_tokenizer.py. The synthetic test fixture's expected token IDs were
generated with that pinned Python reference and regex 2025.11.3. No upstream
inference engine is linked or invoked by Kuno's Rust tokenizer.

