The separate cpu_expert::native backend ports the MIT GGML native CPU Q8_K
quantizer and IQ2_S/IQ3_XXS/IQ3_S/IQ4_XS/IQ4_NL integer equations from llama.cpp
3cf03257f219afbe7334045ff7c6a06ac68c627d, the ggml revision pinned by MIT Strata
fb58e0dbc8399662c0e47c76578c6e878b14f6cf. Its ID42 Q2_0 path follows Strata's
CPU Q8_1 activation rounding and original four-code signed layout. Runtime is
Rust; no ggml or Strata C/C++ engine/library is linked. Existing public GGML
codebook attribution and license below/above continue to apply. Native SIMD
integer sums are exact; floating-point multi-token reduction parity remains an
explicit validation gate rather than an original64 arithmetic claim.
